/-!
# Two movers, frozen readings [1, 3, 4, 6, 7]: the landing for ALL movers beyond the least frozen reading, in whichever lonely piece holds it (GENERATED by `s2later_gen_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  Lonely pieces of the frozen set from `1/(8·1)` (exact), indexed from 0: {1/8}, [3/16, 7/32], [3/8, 23/56], [25/56, 15/32], [17/32, 31/56].
* `landL13467_<j>`: for ANY `d1, d2 > 0`, IF no piece `i < j` holds a common clear instant of the two movers and piece `j` does, THEN the first lonely
  instant `T` of the frozen set with both movers exists, lies in piece `j`, and is the first common clear instant at or after its left end (the movers-only
  cascade fixed point from the left end of piece `j`).  Earlier pieces are excluded by the hypothesis, the gaps by `fnot`, later pieces by order.
