  box kinds (kind, piece): {"('P', 0)": 15, "('P', 1)": 14, "('P', 2)": 4, "('P', 3)": 2, "('P', 4)": 6, "('R1a', 1)": 18, "('R1a', 2)": 7, "('R1a', 3)": 2, "('R1a', 4)": 2}; `d1 > 28` by `big_both` in piece 2 [PROVISIONAL: counting tool]).
* `land2_later_13467`: the assembled statement, no grid, no upper threshold.  No nonexistence of a common clear instant is proved for any box: the case split is on the
  statement itself (`by_cases` on each piece in turn).
Grades: [L]; the existence statement is discharged by a finite box cover [PROVISIONAL: covering]; `r1_rect`/`big_both` are [PROVISIONAL: counting tool].
Not proved here: the cascade's path inside the piece; movers at or below `1`.
